  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-01-13T20:33:13.310Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This is a new bug that I only discovered last night. Apparently if you block a person or if a blocked user is in the same instance as you, for some odd reason blocking a person reduces frame rate. I think there are 2 reasons as to why this might be happening:\n\n1) The change from having user moderation settings switching from client side to being locally stored on the computer can possibly cause some issues.\n\n2) It is likely that when blocking a user, even though they are disabled and not shown it is likely that disabling their avatar enables every single animation, mesh, audio sources, material swaps, etc. that the blocked user are turned on so that you cannot see anything from them at all.\n\nEither way this is a major issue that needs to be addressed as soon as possible, because the opposite should be happening when blocking users.\n\nHere is a video I took the night that I am posting this showing what is going on:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Smash_ter/status/1613813389834489856\n\nEdit: I recorded what I posted to twitter at around 2:28 AM EST. After looking through the output logs, it is likely that the other possibilities is that VRChat is updating the pose of blocked players, and maybe other things alongside that and actively failing. This is nearly half of the output log. This is a snapshot of my logs and I will provide the full output log to the devs if necessary",
